{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-128014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the minor of ${a}_{12}$ in the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3d & 5b \\\\ b & {c}^{2} & b-d \\\\ b & -10c & b+d\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the first row and second column:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & -3d & ∗ \\\\ b & ∗ & b-d \\\\ b & ∗ & b+d\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}b & b-d \\\\ b & b+d\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}b & b-d \\\\ b & b+d\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =b\\cdot (b+d)-(b-d)\\cdot b \\\\  & ={b}^{2}+bd-{b}^{2}+db \\\\  & =2bd\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e190c333e855850688ad931cdee76a7d34af7ad2b7d8601d9dd703ab3b989bd"} {"question" "q-128014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10cd+5b"] ["math" "2bd"] ["math" "2{b}^{2}+cd"] ["math" "bc+4d"] ["math" "{c}^{2}-{d}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2bd"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of ${d}_{12}$ is $-4$, find all the possible values of $p$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2} & {p}^{3} & 6 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2+p & p-1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the first row and second column:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & {p}^{3} & ∗ \\\\ -6 & ∗ & 5 \\\\ 5 & ∗ & p-1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${d}_{12}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 5 \\\\ 5 & p-1\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 5 \\\\ 5 & p-1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-6\\cdot (p-1)-5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-6p-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${d}_{12}$ is $-4$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6p-19 & =-4 \\\\ -6p & =15 \\\\ p & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p=-\\frac{5}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e190c333e855850688ad931cdee76a7d34af7ad2b7d8601d9dd703ab3b989bd"} {"question" "q-128083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "p=-2"] ["math" "p=-\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "p=7"] ["math" "p=9"] ["math" "p=\\frac{6}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "p=-\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of ${m}_{21}$ is $11$, find all the possible values of $y$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}y & \\frac{3}{2} & y \\\\ 25 & 4-y & 12y \\\\ y & 2 & -6y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and first column:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & \\frac{3}{2} & y \\\\ 25 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 2 & -6y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${m}_{21}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} & y \\\\ 2 & -6y\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} & y \\\\ 2 & -6y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-6y)-y\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-11y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${m}_{21}$ is $11$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-11y & =11 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e190c333e855850688ad931cdee76a7d34af7ad2b7d8601d9dd703ab3b989bd"} {"question" "q-128087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-1"] ["math" "y=-2"] ["math" "y=0"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{7}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-128087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-275530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $17$, find all the possible values of $p$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & p & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & p\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values of $p$ are\n\n$p=$ \n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,p=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-275530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{11},$ we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & p & 4 \\\\ ∗ & -2 & p\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}p & 4 \\\\ -2 & p\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 4 \\\\ -2 & p\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =p\\cdot p-4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ={p}^{2}+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $17$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}+8 & =17 \\\\ {p}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ (p-3)(p+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $p=-3$ and $p=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-275530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e190c333e855850688ad931cdee76a7d34af7ad2b7d8601d9dd703ab3b989bd"} {"question" "q-275530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-275530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-275530" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-275530" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-319175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the matrix\n$T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & e & f \\\\ 5 & 3d & 2 \\\\ 4 & 7 & d\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{31}$ of the element ${t}_{31}.$\n\n${M}_{31}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-319175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate the minor of ${t}_{31},$ we remove the third row and first column:\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & e & f \\\\ ∗ & 3d & 2 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${t}_{31}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{31} & =det[\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ 3d & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ 3d & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =e\\cdot 2-f\\cdot (3d) \\\\  & =2e-3df.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-319175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9e190c333e855850688ad931cdee76a7d34af7ad2b7d8601d9dd703ab3b989bd"} {"question" "q-319175" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"} {"question" "q-319175" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2e-3df"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979306/state.json" "file_sha256" "83f2df6e22d339fab0dc2f0e220972aacba22c61f08c1eed1b601e6a9262a564"}] "usage" {} "basis" 852 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
